sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2011) PRL & Shyer et al. (2013) Science sequential smooth-muscle mucosal buckling into ridges, zigzags, and hexagonal villi — MorphoEval overall 87.8/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 (v3) re-score of `2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py` (overall 87.8/100, down from 93.1 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed in a reduced, clearly labelled form: the flat Winkler bed is replaced by a Lamé-verified axisymmetric neo-Hookean ring FEM of the mesenchymal annulus (K_eff, curvature factor 0.88-0.93, integer mode quantisation reproducing 10/12/16/19/26 vs 10/12/16/19/25 observed ridges, Donnell gamma per stage), and a curvature-driven Shh/BMP mesenchymal-cluster field localises the apicobasal cubic gain at zigzag elbows (E14 elbow index 1.42) and villus tips (E16 1.19 clusters per villus) with a 5.9 um elbow bulge absent in the `--no-shh-bmp` ablation; three new Lean theorems (6 total, 0 sorrys), 8 new measurements (17 total), 4 new self-test checks (12 total), 2 new SHA-pinned dataset files and a new 4-panel figure accompany it. The score falls because the current code shows that stage amplitude and zigzag angle are prescribed from the observed values (L666-669, L779-782), the surface is blended 85/15 with a prescribed cosine (L732), lambda_sim is 85% analytic (L802), |Psi_6| is a literal per regime (L811-815), the reference moduli were fitted to lambda_obs, and the specimen is a species-unmatched ileum section — defects v2 did not penalise. Overall 87.8/100 (faithfulness 86.0, reproducibility 92.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 89, Reproducibility package 95. Output judged: docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_comparison.png: rendered output of 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py at 45670cb8, image/png, 1135536 B, 2622×1412 px, artifact_sha256 a1cc184d192301cde6a1045c99e0774008edf896123bc90cac8a1251cb7ea1a5 (sha256 a1cc184d192301cde6a1045c99e0774008edf896123bc90cac8a1251cb7ea1a5), spec_fingerprint da01f54f3142bab9fe39c5f26bd338e06f8c4d88ac4dfcc5ab72c0d0def8016a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: da01f54f3142bab9fe39c5f26bd338e06f8c4d88ac4dfcc5ab72c0d0def8016a; artifact_sha256: a1cc184d192301cde6a1045c99e0774008edf896123bc90cac8a1251cb7ea1a5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_reference.json=1887bf2160034e33..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/intestinal_villi_crypts_specimen.jpg=30afcb789bbdc60c..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/paper_citations.bib=a8bc0251af8be542..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/pass3_citations.bib=38af06185530b95f..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/scout_manifest.json=1e6e1bbc98fb4873..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/tubular_shh_bmp_reference.json=c3f1b76b4c31b3a1...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-crypt-villus-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Shyer et al. (2013): sequential differentiation of circumferential, longitudinal and second circumferential smooth-muscle layers compresses the chick gut mucosa into longitudinal ridges (E8-E10), herringbone zigzags (E13-E14) and a hexagonal array of villi (E16); FK506 muscle inhibition and surgical slitting arrest the cascade at the preceding regime; the wavelength scales as a quartic length (B_e/K_s)^(1/4) across chick, quail and mouse | Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2011): buckling of a monolayered epithelium on an elastic stroma with wavenumber q_* = (K_s/B_e)^(1/4) and an apicobasal cubic term that selects finger-like protrusions over invaginations | Walton et al. (2012, 2016) and Shyer et al. (2015): Hh-responsive mesenchymal clusters localise under the epithelium at the tips of emerging villi (mouse) and at the high-curvature elbows of zigzags (chick), with BMP signalling from the clusters | Timoshenko & Goodier (1970) §28 and Donnell (1933): the Lamé thick-walled cylinder displacement u = A r + B/r and the shell curvature parameter that controls when a flat-plate (FvK) reduction of a thin cylindrical shell is valid; reconstructed_in_script: Mucosal bending rigidity B_e, Winkler foundation K_s, quartic length ell_* and a 4-regime classifier; a 64^2 pseudo-spectral FvK free energy minimised by L-BFGS-B (65 iterations) then blended with a prescribed cosine; a 48-element axisymmetric plane-strain ring FEM of the mesenchymal annulus with rigid outer (smooth-muscle) wall giving K_tube, slab limit, curvature factor and optional neo-Hookean prestrain tangent; integer mode quantisation n = round(2 pi R / lambda) and the Donnell ratio per stage; an OLS-through-origin tube prefactor c_tube = 0.5513; a curvature-driven Shh field, percentile-thresholded cluster indicator, localized cubic gain and a linear spectral Newton response with a 30% trust region; a 12-point 3-species wavelength collapse; 5 FK506/surgical controls; DoG + Delaunay segmentation of the vendored specimen; 17 reference-anchored measurements; transfer_boundary: The tubular coupling is a 1D-radial axisymmetric FEM feeding a scalar K_eff into the 2D flat FvK sheet, not a 3D non-axisymmetric tubular neo-Hookean solid; the Donnell ratio itself says the flat reduction is only well justified from E13 on (gamma 0.65 at E8) | Stage amplitudes, zigzag angles and |Psi_6| are prescribed from the observed values (or literals) rather than emerging from the minimiser, so the amplitude, theta and |Psi_6| 'measurements' are templated; the reported lambda_sim is 0.85 lambda_* + 0.15 lambda_fft | The stage-resolved E_e, E_s, H_s, epsilon_x, epsilon_y, alpha_3 in epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_reference.json were fitted so that the flat model with C_LAMBDA_PREFACTOR = 0.5690 reproduces lambda_obs; the r = 0.9996 collapse inherits that fit | The Shh field is curvature-driven (no Ptch1/Gli reaction-diffusion); elbow curvature is proxied by crest-contour turning curvature because the prescribed developable surface has no preferential elbow dome curvature; cluster-enrichment references are qualitative (null = 1.0) | The SHA-pinned specimen is a CC0 terminal-ileum H&E cross-section of unknown species and age, compared with chick E16 hexagonal order without a pixel scale; does_not_claim: A full 3D tubular neo-Hookean finite-element solution, emergent (unprescribed) stage amplitudes or zigzag angles, a reaction-diffusion Shh/BMP/Ptch1 network, finite smooth-muscle sheath stiffness, species-matched specimen histology, or empirically measured stage-resolved mesenchymal moduli." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py:1101-1188 — the SHA-pinned specimen is a terminal-ileum H&E section of unknown species/age compared with chick E16 hexagonal order via a hard-coded ROI [60:660, 80:880], DoG sigmas 18/45, percentiles 28/55 and Delaunay edge bounds 40-185 px with no pixel scale. Vendor a chick E16 (or quail/mouse) villus-field micrograph with a scale bar and derive the detection scales from the expected villus spacing.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py:290-365 (rigid outer wall u(R_out)=0) and 261-271 — the ring FEM is axisymmetric and 1D-radial, and the smooth-muscle sheath is infinitely stiff; the v2 item asked for a 3D tubular neo-Hookean mesh. Add a finite muscle-spring boundary (E_m h_m/R^2) and extend the foundation to a non-axisymmetric (r, theta) mesh so the curvature factor depends on the circumferential mode n.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py:422-484 and 136-142 — the Shh field is curvature-driven with five tunables (SHH_BMP_CUBIC_GAIN 0.60, ELBOW_DOME_GAIN 1.0, SHH_CLUSTER_QUANTILE 0.82, SHH_TRUST_FRACTION 0.30, diffusion_length_frac 0.16) that have no empirical anchor, and the docstring admits a direct Shyer-2015 exp(-d/ell) test gives elbow index < 1 on the developable surface. Replace the curvature proxy by a Shh/Ptch1/BMP reaction-diffusion model on the deformed surface and anchor the cluster spacing to Walton 2012 / Shyer 2015 measured cluster counts.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py:666-669, 677 and 732 — theta_zz is taken from target_theta_zz_deg (observed, unsourced 0.92 fallback), the hexagonal angle is the literal 58.5, and the relaxed surface is blended 0.85 prescribed cosine + 0.15 relaxed, so the 'E14 theta_zz = 38.5 vs 38.5' measurement is templated. Remove the blend and the target, and measure theta_zz from the crest contours of the relaxed surface.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py:722 and 748-770 — L-BFGS-B stops on its 65-iteration limit because L_op^2 has condition number ~1e7 on the 64^2 grid, which is why Pass 3 uses a linear Newton response instead of re-minimising. Replace the minimiser by a semi-implicit (exponential-integrator) spectral gradient flow on the FvK energy so the cluster-coupled surface is a true energy minimum.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py:779-782 and 877, 1075 — the stage amplitude is rescaled to target_amplitude_um = the observed amplitude_obs_um, so Panel D, the GIF amplitude curves and the FK506 amplitude comparisons are circular; the non-target fallback 155*sqrt(dex+0.8 dey) is unsourced. Let the amplitude emerge from the minimiser (or from the weakly nonlinear amplitude equation A^2 ~ (mu - mu_c)/g) and compare the prediction with amplitude_obs_um as a genuine measurement.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py:802 and 811-815 — lambda_sim = 0.85 lambda_* + 0.15 lambda_fft and psi6_sim is a per-regime literal (0.09 / 0.28 + 0.10 dey/dex / 0.78), so the E16 |Psi_6| = 0.78 vs 0.78 measurement is self-referential. Report lambda_fft as the simulated wavelength and compute |Psi_6| from the Delaunay neighbourhood of the detected villus maxima, as is already done for the specimen (L1101-1188).",
            "remediation needed: datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_reference.json and 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py:127, 965-983 — the stage-resolved E_e, E_s, H_s, epsilon_x, epsilon_y, alpha_3 were fitted so that the flat model with C_LAMBDA_PREFACTOR = 0.5690 reproduces lambda_obs, and c_tube is an OLS fit to the same data, so the flat and tube RMSE and the 12-point collapse are in-sample. Source stage moduli and thicknesses from Shyer 2013 SM measurements (or state them as fitted) and hold out at least one species for the collapse." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.878"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 063 Pass 3 Phase B Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

